   "cooked": "<h2>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#friday-9-july-2021-1\" name=\"friday-9-july-2021-1\"></a><strong>Friday, 9 July 2021</strong>\n</h2>\n<p>Welcome to our weekly update! Join us in real time during any of our many call. Check out <a>the calendar</a>.</p>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#reminder-the-tec-will-be-in-paris-for-ethcc-4httpsethccio-july-20-22-2\" name=\"reminder-the-tec-will-be-in-paris-for-ethcc-4httpsethccio-july-20-22-2\"></a><strong>REMINDER:</strong> the TEC will be in Paris for <a href=\"https://ethcc.io/\">EthCC 4</a> July 20-22!</h3>\n<p>Let us know if you’ll be there too, come say hi on our Discord <span class=\"hashtag\">#community-hall</span> channel.</p>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#comms-3\" name=\"comms-3\"></a><img alt=\":satellite:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/satellite.png?v=9\" title=\":satellite:\"/> Comms</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Signalled ready for Hatch! (See Stewards below for the signal of each WG.)</li>\n<li>Released our <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vf1rOMDzw38\">community video!</a> All over the world, the Token Engineering Commons is preparing for the Hatch. Get to know some of our Stewards and Subject Matter Experts who compose this community.</li>\n<li>TE Scouts held two TEC sessions this week: one at <a href=\"https://gov.gitcoin.co/t/you-are-invited-to-come-party-with-the-token-engineering-commons-dao/7784\">Gitcoin</a> and the other at Metagame.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Forum Highlight</strong>: <a href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/t/how-to-get-wxdai-a-bridging-story/347\">How to get wxDAI</a>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#commons-swarm-4\" name=\"commons-swarm-4\"></a><img alt=\":globe_with_meridians:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/globe_with_meridians.png?v=9\" title=\":globe_with_meridians:\"/> Commons Swarm</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>The <a href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/t/hatch-dress-rehearshal-recap/471\">dress rehearsal recap</a> summarizes the process of test tokens going through the smart contracts: mintings, impact hours, ragequitting, and the “commons” upgrade.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Forum Highlight</strong>: <a href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/t/commons-swarm-how-are-we-doing/327/14\">Weekly update</a>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#gravity-5\" name=\"gravity-5\"></a><img alt=\":dove:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/dove.png?v=9\" title=\":dove:\"/> Gravity</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>We are working on the next round of Graviton trainings for September! More details soon.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#hatch-outreach-6\" name=\"hatch-outreach-6\"></a>🏄‍♂️ Hatch Outreach</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>A Hatcher Checklist is coming out soon with all the boxes to check to confirm your Hatcher readiness!</li>\n<li>The Hatcher Handbook will follow with more details about the steps to get there.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#labs-7\" name=\"labs-7\"></a><img alt=\":microscope:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/microscope.png?v=9\" title=\":microscope:\"/> Labs</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Labs’ Steward Ygg contributed an Impact Hour/Praise intervention proposal to serve as a possible implementation of <a href=\"https://github.com/CommonsBuild/IH-intervention/issues/11\">Praisemageddon</a>, one of the two chosen IH intervention proposals from the run-off vote. <a href=\"https://github.com/CommonsBuild/IH-intervention/issues/15\">The Best Intervention: Composite Augmentation</a>. (See SoftGov below for more on the run-off vote results.)</li>\n<li>TokenSPICE in development! TokenSPICE can be used to help design, tune and verify tokenized ecosystems in an overall token engineering flow. Join us on Saturdays at 8pm PST / 5am+1 CET.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#legal-8\" name=\"legal-8\"></a><img alt=\":classical_building:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/classical_building.png?v=9\" title=\":classical_building:\"/> Legal</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Working on the Community Covenant, the rules by which we must agree to in order to engage in the community.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#0mega-9\" name=\"0mega-9\"></a><img alt=\":dizzy:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/dizzy.png?v=9\" title=\":dizzy:\"/> 0mega</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Next meeting will be 21st July 8PM CET.\n<ul>\n<li>Structure TE Ethics topics</li>\n<li>Timeline for focus groups</li>\n<li>Useful results processing</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#params-10\" name=\"params-10\"></a><img alt=\":robot:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/robot.png?v=9\" title=\":robot:\"/> Params</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Commons Configuration Dashboard:\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.figma.com/proto/b6kx4mkaHxzq4TPzaI1eRY/TEC-Dapps?page-id=3370%3A14921&amp;node-id=3413%3A15145&amp;viewport=-1613%2C-87%2C0.1384066492319107&amp;scaling=min-zoom\">Design Validation</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://bondingcurve.herokuapp.com/app\">Python Backend</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/c/defi-legos-and-how-they-work-together/ccd-params/26\">Param Documentation</a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#soft-gov-11\" name=\"soft-gov-11\"></a><img alt=\":raised_hands:t4:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/raised_hands/4.png?v=9\" title=\":raised_hands:t4:\"/> Soft Gov</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Final votes were cast July 8 for the run-off vote of the Impact Hour/Praise intervention. The vote resulted in two top propopals taking a vast majority of the votes between them. Read Griff’s explanation for a solution on the <a href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/t/pre-hatch-impact-hours-distribution-analysis/376/84\">Pre-Hatch Impact Hours Distribution Analysis</a> (comment 79 of 81). The two proposals are both being chosen and will be integrated and implemented collectively:<br/>\n<strong><span class=\"hashtag\">#11</span></strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/CommonsBuild/IH-intervention/issues/11\"><img alt=\":fire:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/fire.png?v=9\" title=\":fire:\"/> PRAISEMAGEDDON <img alt=\":fire:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/fire.png?v=9\" title=\":fire:\"/></a><br/>\n<strong><span class=\"hashtag\">#12</span></strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/CommonsBuild/IH-intervention/issues/12\"><img alt=\":alien:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/alien.png?v=9\" title=\":alien:\"/> No Abnormal Intervention <img alt=\":alien:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/alien.png?v=9\" title=\":alien:\"/> <img alt=\":no_entry_sign:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/no_entry_sign.png?v=9\" title=\":no_entry_sign:\"/> 75% Governance Rights returned to paid contributors via vote Post-Hatch &amp; Praise Party for TE Rockstars</a>\n</li>\n<li>TE Book Club re-started July 4 by <strong>!witwiki</strong> reading Ostrom’s <em>Governing the Commons</em> at <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/810180621930070088/810180622165213218/861046719956516874\">The DAO bookclub Discord</a>.</li>\n<li>This week’s SoftGov call held a space for discussing decision-making policies. You can read <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1R8yLfht6GvGHr8VDvyZ-sVP1s54rPLY4MtXPBOqHtO0/edit#heading=h.530p007q2hz6\">participants’ comments in the agenda</a>.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Forum Highlight</strong>: <a href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/t/pre-hatch-impact-hours-distribution-analysis/376\">Pre-Hatch Impact Hours Distribution Analysis</a><br/>\nThis is the longest on-going forum post in the history of the TEC, with 81 comments over two months and counting!</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#stewards-12\" name=\"stewards-12\"></a><img alt=\":ear_of_rice:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/ear_of_rice.png?v=9\" title=\":ear_of_rice:\"/> Stewards</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://hackmd.io/@KNlVuZ6DRninKfubrrwtzg/r1590is3O\">Transparency of the Impact Hour Intervention voting process</a></li>\n<li>Some community stats:\n<ul>\n<li>11 Working Groups</li>\n<li>16 Stewards</li>\n<li>Over 550 participants in the TEC</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Working Group checklist as they become “ready for Hatch”:</li>\n</ul>\n<p></p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" data-download-href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/005434d71bfd509025cb78a002fddd3f292d5840\" href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/original/1X/005434d71bfd509025cb78a002fddd3f292d5840.png\" title=\"\"><img alt=\"\" data-base62-sha1=\"2Upvp5KdCGBckV7fwn7QZrWlpu\" data-small-upload=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/optimized/1X/005434d71bfd509025cb78a002fddd3f292d5840_2_10x10.png\" height=\"450\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/optimized/1X/005434d71bfd509025cb78a002fddd3f292d5840_2_690x450.png\" srcset=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/optimized/1X/005434d71bfd509025cb78a002fddd3f292d5840_2_690x450.png, https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/original/1X/005434d71bfd509025cb78a002fddd3f292d5840.png 1.5x, https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/original/1X/005434d71bfd509025cb78a002fddd3f292d5840.png 2x\" width=\"690\"/><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\"><use xlink:href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\"></span><span class=\"informations\">761×497 72 KB</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\"><use xlink:href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#transparency-13\" name=\"transparency-13\"></a><img alt=\":male_detective:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/male_detective.png?v=9\" title=\":male_detective:\"/> Transparency</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>Forum highlight</strong>: <a href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/t/using-dashlane-as-tec-credentials-manager/478\">Using Dashlane as TEC credentials manager</a>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr/>\n<p>Thanks for reading! <img alt=\":blue_book:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/blue_book.png?v=9\" title=\":blue_book:\"/> See you soon! <img alt=\":wave:t5:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/wave/5.png?v=9\" title=\":wave:t5:\"/></p>",
